From 6db77afaac06e35a281b73e97804155f3af543e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:24:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FIX-173: native regions take in only the bytes the CPU
 changed

GT Sport computes the cockpit's light from its interior capture into 64 bytes
at 0x1000e317c0 every third frame (cs 0xa82d2fe / 0x94c7c466), read by the car
interior shaders. Native keeps GPU-written ranges in VRAM regions (NAT-144),
and the CPU writes other data in that 4 KB page every frame: each write fault
copied the whole page from guest memory into the region, putting stale bytes
over the GPU's result, so the cockpit was lit in one frame of three and dark
in the other two (Lance's Tokyo video). The same clobbering also hit other
GPU-written data: frame dumps that showed the sky as a flat bright patch over
the buildings (2 of 6) are clean now.

OnCpuWrite now keeps a copy of region pages (writes up to 64 KB) as they were
before the write; RefreshRegion watches the page again first, then copies in
only the 16-byte pieces that differ from that copy. Regions taken in by a
bigger one keep their pending CPU writes. Tokyo race: single-frame cockpit
flashes 6.7% -> 0.4% of frames, ~12% of refreshed page bytes copied, 48.2 fps
(48.0 before).

Diagnosis switches added on the way (all off by default):
- FIX-170 RYGT_NATIVE_SNAPSHOT_BELOW=<bytes>: small read-only shader buffers
  copied when the draw is recorded instead of read in place.
- FIX-171 RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_EVERY=<frames> and RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_RECT=x,y,w,h
  for the RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_TEXTURE probes: per-frame GPU readbacks, untiled
  per mip/layer means of B10G11R11 pictures, thirds of plain pictures.
- FIX-172 RYGT_NATIVE_INPLACE_RANGES=<hex>+<hex>,...: written ranges kept in
  guest memory.
- FIX-174 RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_BUFFER=<hex>+<hex>: shaders binding that range.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
